# sh-to-py C5: research/eval pipeline

Part of the sh-to-py bash-to-Python migration (umbrella tracking issue links all parts).

**Goal**: Port /research support machinery and the research evaluation harness.

**Absorbs (approx lines)**: skills/research/scripts/validate-citations.sh (975; 5 .md refs), render-findings-batch.sh (517; 3 .md refs), run-research-planner.sh (182; 3 .md refs), compute-research-banner.sh (72); scripts/validate-research-output.sh (557), eval-research.sh (735), dialectic-smoke-test.sh (465).

**Notes**: planner launch reuses B4; findings rendering reuses B6. Harnesses test-render-findings-batch.sh, test-validate-research-output.sh port to pytest here.

**Dependencies (wired natively via /block-issue)**: B4, B6.

**Definition of done**: importable functions; CLI verbs in python/cli.py; direct call-site cutover (no shims); pytest replaces harness coverage; absorbed bash + harnesses deleted; stale-reference sweep; make lint + py-lint + py-test green.

</feature_description>


